{
  "name": "Error alerts for all your n8n workflows (Telegram)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Error alerts on Telegram\nSends you a Telegram message whenever another workflow fails, with the workflow name, the node that failed, the error and a link to the execution.\n\n1. Add your Telegram bot credential and your chat ID in **Send alert**.\n2. Save and activate this workflow.\n3. In each workflow you want covered, open Settings and pick this workflow as the **Error workflow**.\n\nFree template by [serverserv](https://serverserv.com/n8n-templates.html). MIT licence.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "00473f9c-8729-59da-bf15-54ed9ff20260",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -140,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "bc4d1a82-a2a5-57ff-8755-75fbbe434c5b",
      "name": "When a workflow fails",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "123456789",
        "text": "=Workflow failed: {{ $json.workflow.name }}\nNode: {{ $json.execution.lastNodeExecuted || 'unknown' }}\nError: {{ ($json.execution.error && $json.execution.error.message || 'no message').slice(0, 500) }}\n{{ $json.execution.url || '' }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "325e25fa-9b0a-57dd-b2a4-22de68974cd8",
      "name": "Send alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
